{
 "_comment": "Qwen-Image-Edit 2511 + 4-step Lightning + optional style LoRA, driven by TextEncodeQwenImageEditPlus with up to 3 REFERENCE images. This is the character-consistency workflow: instead of re-describing a character in words on every shot (which re-invents the face every time), you hand it a canonical character sheet and ask for a new scene.",
 "_notes": [
  "Node 20 is the target latent. Node 12 encodes reference 1 instead. Swap 13.inputs.latent_image between them to choose REFERENCE mode (20, empty latent, denoise 1.0) or EDIT mode (12, the reference is the canvas).",
  "image1 on nodes 10/11 is the character sheet. image2/image3 pin a second character or a location plate.",
  "The 2511 Lightning LoRA takes editing from ~48s to ~6s, which is the difference between reference-locked keyframes being unaffordable and being the default.",
  "Negative prompt gets the same references, per the Qwen edit convention."
 ],
